{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cfbr7Mvy92FjDi15ryQWC", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags here are a simple TOML file plus one helper, and the code matches what the project's notes say.\n\n**How it works**\n- `flags.toml` has a `[flags]` table of `name = bool` entries. The only flag now is `invoice-pdf-v2 = false`.\n- `src/flags.py` loads that file once at import time. `flags.is_on(\"name\")` returns the flag's value as a bool, and `all_flags()` returns a copy of the whole table.\n- The value is read at import, so changing a flag means editing `flags.toml` and restarting. There is no per-environment override in the code. The notes say flags can be turned on per environment without a deploy, but I didn't find where that happens. It may be handled outside this repo, such as a different `flags.toml` per environment, so check that before relying on it.\n\n**Conventions**\n- Read flags only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")`. Don't parse the TOML yourself.\n- Names are kebab-case.\n- Declare the flag in `flags.toml` before any code reads it. An undeclared name makes `is_on()` return `False` with no error, so a typo in the name leaves the new flow permanently off.\n\n**For the checkout flow**\n1. Add `new-checkout-flow = false` (or a name you prefer) to `flags.toml`.\n2. At the entry point, branch on `flags.is_on(\"new-checkout-flow\")`, with the old flow as the else path.\n3. Turn it on by setting the flag to `true` in the target environment's config.\n\nWant me to add the flag and wire up the branch? If so, tell me which module holds the current checkout entry point. I didn't look for it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 437, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24742, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 437}, "output_tokens": 529,